{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268559Z","id":"1a87bb936cc9a3b66eb41bcf9065c2243c48d83f6198b35758e07b56fe42c21f","body":{"detail":"The widget tests cover a make that succeeds, network cuts, notice taps and a landed change. The other exits from _makeApp (lib/app.dart:500-511) and _onWorker's RunQuiet branch are the ones that would leave the ongoing notification and the service running if they regressed.","kind":"suggestion","summary":"Test that a cancelled make, a failed make, and a change that ends cancelled or interrupted each stop the service","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.450675Z","id":"f732e4e0c04fad84f43df8603c218f9e79bf143d52e1ca5d0bab39419776fad4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Added 'a cancelled make stops the service and posts nothing, even in the background', 'a failed make stops the service', 'a change cut off by quitting stops the service and posts nothing' and 'an interrupted change stops the service and posts nothing'. Evidence: flutter test test/app_background_test.dart -> +11, all passed.","supersedes":"1a87bb936cc9a3b66eb41bcf9065c2243c48d83f6198b35758e07b56fe42c21f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:17.325604Z","id":"be6821efcbe6e33f4cb93839309645baa1a1429b2a0752a520bdc1805afee81b","body":{"detail":"Failure: at f1c07f346b12 (a clean detached checkout), `flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart` ends +44 -2: 'a make the last run never finished is offered again at launch' and 'Not now forgets the lost make' fail, because the committed file asserts the 'Make it again?' dialog that f1c07f346b12 replaced with interrupted tiles. The committed file also drops 'a question asked in the background is posted; its tap shows the question sheet' and the _QuestionPage questionPage override. The tests this file should carry ('coming back without tapping the notification shows a question still open in the sheet…', 'a background question about another app is told in a toast on return…') exist only in the uncommitted working tree; `git diff f1c07f346b12^ -- apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart` on that tree shows only them and the _QuestionPage loads list, and with it the suite passes (+49). Against f1c07f346b12^ lib/app.dart those two tests and app_test.dart's 'questions asked while the sheet shows one wait…' fail, as they should. Fix: commit the working-tree file alone.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":425},"end":{"line":518},"content_hash":"e0a9fd9f21ad63537a5c8d2f328573d6262820214b8a3e15586fccce4c615d1f"},"summary":"Commit f1c07f346b12 put a stale app_background_test.dart in history: it deletes the existing background-question test, reverts the lost-make tests to the old launch dialog, and lacks the two return-to-foreground question tests; the intended file is uncommitted","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:12:11.242865Z","id":"eacf3a23558b01352b12f2d4fb8e681993131179d173155eaa1f3124adc889dd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: f1c07f346b12 commits the intended app_background_test.dart (the background-question tap test kept, the lost-make tests as f1c07f346b12 left them, the two return-to-foreground tests added). flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +49, All tests passed.","supersedes":"be6821efcbe6e33f4cb93839309645baa1a1429b2a0752a520bdc1805afee81b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_remote_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:24:13.070244Z","id":"a909e9bbf47f806d17f252dd6665bf554c56ee5b304864f7135a3fafc33d2368","body":{"detail":"The loop runs tester.runAsync(Future.delayed(Duration.zero)) and pump(100 ms) 20 times, then expects heads() == before + 1. LineageStore reads files with asynchronous IO in real time, so under load the checker's single read may not have happened after 20 zero-length turns (a false failure), and a duplicate read that lands after the 20th turn (the double fetch the test is named for) is never seen.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":195},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"cf1b5c8fdc23b0111f18374b858bb0871a372f5b39ecb1fbe454b5f84ae8053b"},"suggested_fix":"Await the checker's work directly (expose LinkedChecker through AppServices, or wait for status to hold the app) before counting, then pump further and count again.","summary":"'a linked app opened reads its head once' waits a fixed 20 event-loop turns, then checks the count: a second read after the loop passes, and slow file IO under load fails it","tags":["area:remote","test","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_remote_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:33:26.642979Z","id":"7942e69a6bfcacc49d8caf92316eb420a2b5c481acfce71990a2c3b4c23679d0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d30518a83","summary":"The test waits until the open app screen's LinkedAppHooks.status holds the app's head (pumpUntil, a condition), counts head reads, pumps further and checks the count and that the status object is unchanged. With the opened hook in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart made to start a second onOpen after the first, it fails (Expected <2>, Actual <3>); restored, //apps/clax_app:app_remote_test PASSED at d30518a83.","supersedes":"a909e9bbf47f806d17f252dd6665bf554c56ee5b304864f7135a3fafc33d2368","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/app_remote_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:06.461294Z","id":"bf842c64dcbbddf9399a1ec5ede393279dc5cc775ab52ed8f33ced4b6e6c752b","body":{"detail":"pumpUntil checks its condition, then runs tester.runAsync(Future.delayed(Duration.zero)) and pump(10 ms) up to 400 times before failing. The conditions it waits on (held-replies writes, lineage reads, head reads) complete through asynchronous file IO in real time, so the number of turns they take grows with machine load; the bound behaves as a wall-clock budget of a few hundred milliseconds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"7cae10de7c88045998d93f47fa7ab0dd805ee38a2b4606ad77b013cbd2434061"},"suggested_fix":"Where the condition has a future (a HeldReplies write, a checker status change), await it inside tester.runAsync instead of counting turns; keep turn counts only for checks of absence.","summary":"pumpUntil's bound of 400 zero-length real turns is a hidden time budget: file IO slower than 400 turns under load fails the test","tags":["area:remote","test","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
